                        "source_sense_description": "Un peu fou.",
                        "target_lang_word": "einen an der Klatsche haben",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "einen an der Klatsche haben",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ece4da72-1dcd-36de-8022-265b7c6eb7b4",
                                        "entry_id": "563021f6-a0f9-3249-864a-cdd88eff14ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(auf den Sprechenden) geistig verwirrt erscheinen; verrückt sein"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "casual",
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "640cf7b7-30af-41d4-8d27-896e57e00139",
                                                "sense_id": "ece4da72-1dcd-36de-8022-265b7c6eb7b4",
                                                "text": "Es ist sinnlos, mit dir noch weiter zu reden. Du hast doch einen an der Klatsche!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88623bb7-42ef-45ca-8707-573c29cc1269",
                                                "sense_id": "ece4da72-1dcd-36de-8022-265b7c6eb7b4",
                                                "text": "Unser neuer Kollege führt ständig Selbstgespräche. Der scheint einen an der Klatsche zu haben."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75d1765b-43ca-40f8-88b5-e9e0e10f2075",
                                                "sense_id": "ece4da72-1dcd-36de-8022-265b7c6eb7b4",
                                                "text": "Man muss schon komplett einen an der Klatsche haben, wenn man im Winter allein im Hochgebirge wandern geht."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67544dd6-de07-4a9b-87ab-d29ba73b1495",
                        "source_entry_id": "66d1e56a-e765-396b-8fc4-8c0233c27464",
                        "source_sense_description": "Un peu fou.",
                        "target_lang_word": "touched",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "touched",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5020e8d-a96d-3e92-9569-8b99b0ca6114",
                                        "entry_id": "98cfeffe-dbb4-3fba-9a5a-0cde1a6c7c2d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Emotionally moved (by), made to feel emotion (by)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce9d0dfa-1ed9-450f-88d7-cf0bd0c5d9e1",
                                                "sense_id": "c5020e8d-a96d-3e92-9569-8b99b0ca6114",
                                                "text": "I was touched that he should remember my birthday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9f8c21d-3900-49f8-b777-140ba93c988a",
                                                "sense_id": "c5020e8d-a96d-3e92-9569-8b99b0ca6114",
                                                "text": "\"They say her Majesty is more touched about these affairs of the Chartists than anything else,\" said Mr Egerton."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "728376b5-74a6-4c9f-8bde-266c6a03ffc6",
                                                "sense_id": "c5020e8d-a96d-3e92-9569-8b99b0ca6114",
                                                "text": "“If there is anything good or true in what I write, it isn’t mine. I owe it all to you and Mother and Beth,” said Jo, more touched by her father’s words than by any amount of praise from the world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc80fbe1-ed0a-45e9-b753-06b20d869317",
                                                "sense_id": "c5020e8d-a96d-3e92-9569-8b99b0ca6114",
                                                "text": "1883, Jules Verne, Mary de Hauteville (translator), The Green Ray, Chapter XXI: A Tempest in a Cavern,\n“And you came to save me, Mr. Oliver,” answered Miss Campbell, more touched by the courage of the young man than the dangers which could still happen."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f480a773-bb72-3f9e-ab94-b72199e4a2bb",
                                        "entry_id": "98cfeffe-dbb4-3fba-9a5a-0cde1a6c7c2d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Slightly mentally deficient; touched in the head."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7d2f2d3-73d5-4fce-a13a-ac70b0f7394a",
                                                "sense_id": "f480a773-bb72-3f9e-ab94-b72199e4a2bb",
                                                "text": "\"Don't you see he is a lunatic, prince?\" whispered Evgenie Pavlovitch in his ear. \"Someone told me just now that he is a bit touched on the subject of lawyers, that he has a mania for making speeches and intends to pass the examinations. I am expecting a splendid burlesque now.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b54bb544-a82f-41d4-a7b9-4f5d73623cf0",
                                                "sense_id": "f480a773-bb72-3f9e-ab94-b72199e4a2bb",
                                                "text": "All a bit touched. Mad Fanny and his other sister Mrs Dickinson driving about with scarlet harness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "442d797d-1ad7-4e4f-bb02-cdbee5e3845a",
                                                "sense_id": "f480a773-bb72-3f9e-ab94-b72199e4a2bb",
                                                "text": "The girl’s face is dreamy, slow. Touched, the Irish say. Possible that she’s touched."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
